---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Crumbs from "../components/Crumbs.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";

const title = "Privacy Policy | MGC Building Ltd";
const description =
  "How MGC Building Ltd uses your name, phone, email and job details when you ask for a quote.";
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <Crumbs items={[{ href: "/", label: "Home" }, { label: "Privacy" }]} />
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p>
        MGC Building Ltd, {site.address.street}, {site.address.locality}, {site.address.region} {site.address.postcode},
        is the business you contact through this site.
      </p>
      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        If you call, email, WhatsApp, or use the quote form, we receive what you send. That is usually your name,
        phone number, email, the town or postcode, and a note about the job. Photos you attach are included.
      </p>
      <h2>Why we use it</h2>
      <p>
        We use those details to reply, book a visit, and send a quote. We do not sell them. We do not use them for a newsletter
        unless you ask to be emailed about a job.
      </p>
      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        We keep quote emails and messages for as long as we need them for the job, the quote, or our own records.
        If you want your details deleted and there is no live job, email {site.email} and ask.
      </p>
      <h2>Who else sees it</h2>
      <p>
        The quote form opens your own email app. It does not send the message through a third-party form service.
        If you email us, your email provider handles the delivery in the normal way.
      </p>
      <h2>The map</h2>
      <p>
        The contact page does not load Google Maps until you press “Show the map”. After that, Google receives the usual
        data a map embed sends. You can also open the address in Google Maps with the link, which leaves this site.
      </p>
      <p>
        Questions: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or <a href={`tel:${site.phoneTel}`}>{site.phoneDisplay}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
